# ── Build artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────
/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.wasm
# Cargo.lock is COMMITTED, deliberately — this is an application (cdylib →
# wasm) with no dependents, not a library. forge.lock pins the deployed wasm
# BY HASH, so a floating Cargo.lock would let one git commit resolve
# different dependency versions and produce a different hash, breaking the
# premise that a hash identifies the code.

# ── Forge CLI credentials & local config (NEVER commit) ───────────
.forge/
forge.toml
config.toml
**/config.toml

# ── Secrets & environment (NEVER commit) ──────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.secret
secrets/
**/credentials*

# ── Customer / seed data dumps (keep real data out of the repo) ───
*.csv
*.dump
*.sqlite
data/local/

# ── OS / editor noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
